test_command=sh tests/rolechecks_test.sh && sh tests/roles_test.sh
id=rolechecks-01 result=green reason=unit test "rolechecks-01: the coder's pre-planning bullet states the id search as a literal grep of the id in the project's test files, keeps passing-or-skipped done-not-redo meaning, and the criterion is observable in tests/" (tests/rolechecks_test.sh) passes -- the bullet now states the search mechanism as "a literal grep of the id in the project's test files (the files carrying the unit-test suite)" (the same fixed string the verifier's code-present bullet uses, per the defined-once/used-identically invariant), HEAD's original sentence survives byte-unchanged with only that mechanism sentence appended, and the criterion is observable in this repo: a literal grep of rolechecks-01 in tests/ finds the run_test name
id=rolechecks-02 result=green reason=unit test "rolechecks-02: the coder's Plan briefly bullet fixes the threshold at more than 8 implementation steps or more than 1 shared contract needing change, drops the is-long wording, and leaves the BLOCKED: stub rule byte-identical" (tests/rolechecks_test.sh) passes -- the bullet states the mechanical fixed threshold (more than 8 implementation steps for one sub-spec, or more than 1 shared contract needing change, marks the change for splitting: flag that the specifier should split it further), the vague "is long" wording is gone from the bullet and the ## Process section, no escape clause or configuration wording appears, and the existing BLOCKED: stub bullet (plain colon, scenario-id tagging) survives byte-identical vs HEAD with ## Process keeping its 9 bullets
id=rolechecks-03 result=green reason=unit test "rolechecks-03: the verifier's Input Rule defines code present mechanically as the shared literal grep finding the declared ids or the result receipt existing, keeps both routing forms, and reads existence only, never the receipt's grammar" (tests/rolechecks_test.sh) passes -- "code present" is now defined mechanically (the same literal grep of the id in the project's test files finds the declared scenario ids, or the result receipt `spdd/changes/<slug>/NN-<feature>.result` exists -- receipt existence only, never its contents, and no receipt-grammar field appears in the Input Rule), the old vague "code changes yet" criterion is gone from the whole prompt, and both routing forms keep their meaning (named form stops reporting nothing to verify; whole-change form verifies every sub-spec with code present and flags the rest as unimplemented rather than stopping outright), with the other two Input Rule bullets byte-identical vs HEAD
id=rolechecks-04 result=green reason=unit test "rolechecks-04: the verifier's merge bullet states one kebab-case spec file per domain resolved from the change README's per-sub-spec section, creates a new domain's file with the Domain header under the same merge rules, and keeps HEAD's merge sentence verbatim" (tests/rolechecks_test.sh) passes -- the bullet states the domain-file rule (one spec file per domain at `spdd/specs/<domain>.md`, kebab-case domain names), the resolution (each sub-spec's destination domain is read from the change README's section for that sub-spec and the merge goes into that domain's file), and the creation rule (new domain: the verifier creates the file with a `# Domain: <domain>` header plus the merged scenarios under the same merge rules), while HEAD's merge-and-never-overwrite sentence survives verbatim inside the extended bullet and the plain-mv and rejected-change bullets are byte-unchanged vs HEAD
id=rolechecks-05 result=green reason=unit test "rolechecks-05: roles-03's exact-string pin is re-scoped to the extended merge bullet while roles-01, roles-02, roles-04, and roles-05 stay byte-identical to HEAD and the whole roles suite passes" (tests/rolechecks_test.sh) passes -- tests/roles_test.sh's test_roles_03 keeps the surviving verbatim pin of the merge sentence alongside new exact-string pins of the extended bullet's content (per-domain file rule, kebab-case naming, README resolution, create-when-new rule), the roles-01/02/04/05 functions are byte-identical vs HEAD, and roles_test.sh runs green end to end (5 passed, including its own surrounding-suite checks); full regression: all 25 tests/*_test.sh suites green with this sub-spec's work in the tree
